  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Omer Courtney Darr was an American sailing master and maritime-tourism pioneer who founded luxury South Pacific schooner cruises. A wartime US Navy veteran, he bought and restored Te Vega, operated passenger voyages between Hawaii and Tahiti, and later captained Wanderer. His demanding ocean passages made him one of the Pacific’s best-known schooner masters.",
